00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:49,240
has a lot less structure than the encoder-decoder. 
So these are the three types we'll go into detail. 

160
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:54,520
Second, the encoder-only is actually not that 
useful in the most general sense. It still has  

161
00:15:54,520 --> 00:16:00,440
some place, but we will just briefly go over 
that, and then spend most of the time comparing  

162
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:07,320
1 and 3. So one has more structure, what's the 
implication of that and so on? So first of all,  

163
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:13,120
let's think about what a transformer is, just 
at a very high level. Or first principles,  

164
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:18,000
what is a transformer? Is a sequence model.
And sequence model is has an input of a  

165
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:23,520
sequence. So sequence can be-- a sequence 
of elements can be words, or images,  

166
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:28,080
or whatever. It's a very general concept. In this 
particular example I show you with the words,  

167
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:32,480
sentence is a sequence of words. And then 
we the first step is to tokenize it because  

168
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:40,600
we have to represent this word in computers 
which requires some kind of encoding scheme,  

169
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:46,280
so we just do it with a fixed number of integers, 
and then we have now a sequence of integers. 

170
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:52,000
And then the dominant paradigm nowadays is to 
represent each sequence element as a vector,  

171
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:57,160
dense vector, because we know how to multiply them 
well. And then so we have a sequence of vectors.  

172
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:04,680
And finally, this sequence model will do the 
following. We just want to model the interaction  

173
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:10,640
between sequence elements. And we do that by let 
them take the dot product of each other. And if  

174
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:15,240
the dot product is high, we can say semantically 
they are more related than the dot products that  

175
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:20,400
is low, and that's kind of the sequence model.
And the transformer is a particular type of  

176
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:29,040
sequence model that uses what's called attention 
to model this interaction . So let's get into the  

177
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:32,800
details of this encoder-decoder, which was 
the original transformer. It's quite many,  

178
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:38,720
many pieces. So let's go into a little bit a piece 
at a time. So starting with the encoder. So here  

179
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:44,480
I'm going to show you an example of machine 
translation, which used to be very cool thing. 

180
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:48,920
And so you are-- you have an English sentence that 
is good, and then we're going to translate it into  

181
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:55,400
German. So first thing is to encode this into a 
dense vector. So here I'm representing it with  

